import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";
---

<StudyLayout>
  <section>
    <h1>Plasma Projector — question test</h1>
    <p>
      11 November 2026. Independent, clean-context, read-only framing review.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="/lab/studies/plasma-projector-2026-11-11"
        >Return to section 01</a
      >
    </p>
    <h2>Results</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>One subject — Pass with findings.</strong>
      Trigger, burst, recovery, recoil and form belong to one fitting. Current
      motion laws need an explicit boundary against the adjacent open motion
      study.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Grounded — Pass with findings.</strong>
      Plasma charge/fire, instant ion contact, destructible fragments and moving
      pirates have code and specification support. Shared weapon funding rules
      were omitted.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Consequence — Pass.</strong>
      One new fitting makes close approach, destructive discharge and recovery a
      distinct manoeuvre.
    </p>
    <h2>Findings and responses</h2>
    <p>
      The Parts contract (docs/specs/game/parts/spec.md, Weapons) and salvage.ts
      funding check establish automatic firing, per-shot spending, zero idle
      draw, the 10% floor and refusal of unaffordable shots. Section 01 now
      preserves that baseline and names a charging exception as a question
      requiring an explicit decision. Automatic trigger timing remains open.
    </p>
    <p>
      The open ship-motion-laws-2026-11-04 study owns motion-law choices.
      Section 01 now fixes current ship-motion laws; projector recoil may use
      them without reopening them. The ships specification establishes mass
      behaviour; rail recoil in salvage.ts supplies available means, not a
      decision about projector recoil or offset mounts.
    </p>
    <p>
      The reviewer noted the opening's length. The three-paragraph framing stays
      compact; the detailed question list is retained deliberately to preserve
      unresolved mechanics and their reasons in this startup record. No
      exploration has been undertaken. Corrections were not reviewed again.
    </p>
    <h2>Evidence and limits</h2>
    <p>
      Grounding: docs/specs/factory/effects/spec.md (plasma light),
      packages/core/src/lib/effects/engine-plume.ts and plasma-plume.ts;
      docs/specs/game/light-ion-cannon/spec.md and
      packages/mode-a/src/lib/salvage.ts (instant contact and fragment
      creation); docs/specs/game/world/derelict/spec.md;
      docs/specs/game/gauntlet/spec.md and packages/mode-a/src/lib/gauntlet.ts
      (independent enemy actors). The full study registry was checked for
      overlap.
    </p>
    <p>
      High cost, devastation, broad brief fire, ten-second recovery and recoil
      are intent or open questions, not implemented behaviour. The reviewer did
      not check rendering, keyboard access, flight readability, balance,
      feasibility, performance or demonstrated escape risk, and ran no tests.
    </p>
  </section>
</StudyLayout>
